// Short screening and interaction diagnosis. Apply with -configuration Release;
// all settings except the four below inherit Release. Keep project/scheme defaults.
// Single-file optimization can change runtime costs: formal acceptance continues
// to use the frozen WMO baseline and final WMO candidate, without a second full
// comparison suite on every batch. Never compare this profile's C with a WMO B.
// Promoting this profile to formal comparison requires new same-profile B/C.
//
// Example screening build, after shared build/runtime work is idle:
// xcodebuild -project MyWallpaperX.xcodeproj -scheme MyWallpaperX -configuration Release -xcconfig script/scene_diagnostic_build.xcconfig -derivedDataPath <isolated-diagnostic-path> -showBuildTimingSummary build
// Existing WMO acceptance build (do not pass this xcconfig):
// xcodebuild -project MyWallpaperX.xcodeproj -scheme MyWallpaperX -configuration Release SWIFT_ACTIVE_COMPILATION_CONDITIONS=DEBUG SWIFT_OPTIMIZATION_LEVEL=-O GCC_OPTIMIZATION_LEVEL=s -derivedDataPath <isolated-wmo-path> build
//
// Reuse the existing build-input freeze and signed App staging/identity chain.
// Record this file's digest, effective compiler settings, Xcode/SDK identity and
// actual Swift/C argv or response files alongside source and App identities.
// Establish first-build, no-op and real-local-edit timings before claiming a
// feedback improvement; WMO/Release runtime acceptance remains separate.

SWIFT_ACTIVE_COMPILATION_CONDITIONS = DEBUG
SWIFT_OPTIMIZATION_LEVEL = -O
GCC_OPTIMIZATION_LEVEL = s
SWIFT_COMPILATION_MODE = singlefile
